url: "https://www.chessmultiverse.org/p/chess-multiverse-error-explorer.html"

abstract: >
  Chess Multiverse Error Explorer is a browser-native analytical platform
  for large-scale research into human chess errors, cognitive collapse
  under time pressure, opening complexity, evaluation-loss modeling,
  and behavioral decision-making patterns. Built on the Chess Multiverse
  Error & Evaluation Dataset (CMEED v1.0), the platform uses DuckDB WASM
  to execute analytical SQL workloads entirely within the browser,
  enabling reproducible computational chess research without requiring
  backend infrastructure.

